---
import ToolLayout from '../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import AdSlot from '../components/AdSlot.astro';
import SignatureCleaner from '../islands/SignatureCleaner';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How do I get a transparent signature PNG?', a: 'Photograph your signature on white paper, open it here, adjust the slider until the paper disappears, and download as <strong>Transparent PNG</strong>. It can be placed on any document without a white box around it.' },
  { q: 'My form needs a JPG under 20KB. Can it do that?', a: 'Yes. Choose <strong>White JPG</strong> and a max size such as 20KB. For exact pixel dimensions, open the result in <a href="/resize-image">Resize Image</a>.' },
  { q: 'Why is my signature faint or broken?', a: 'The slider is removing too much. Move it to the left, or retake the photo with a darker pen and brighter, even light.' },
  { q: 'Should I choose black or blue ink?', a: 'Black is the safest for official forms. Blue makes it obvious the signature was added, not photocopied. “Original” keeps the colour from your photo.' },
  { q: 'Is my signature uploaded?', a: 'No. The photo is processed in your browser and never leaves your device.' },
];
---
<ToolLayout
  slug="signature-cleaner"
  title="Signature Background Remover – Transparent PNG | PDFSherpa"
  description="Turn a phone photo of your signature into clean ink with a transparent or white background. Auto-crop, black or blue ink, KB limits. Free, no upload."
  h1="Signature Cleaner"
  lead="Turn a phone photo of your signature into a crisp, auto-cropped image with a transparent or white background, ready for documents and online forms. It all happens on your device."
  howToTitle="How to Clean Up a Signature"
  steps={['Select a photo of your signature on white paper.', 'Adjust the slider until only the ink remains, and pick an ink colour.', 'Download as transparent PNG or white JPG.']}
  faqs={faqs}
  related={['sign-pdf', 'resize-image', 'compress-image', 'passport-photo-maker']}
>
  <SignatureCleaner client:load />

  <Fragment slot="content">
    <h2>What Signature Cleaner does</h2>
    <p>
      A photo of a signature usually comes with gray paper, shadows and too much empty space. Signature Cleaner removes the paper, keeps the ink with smooth edges,
      crops tightly around it, and can recolour it to solid black or blue. The result looks like you signed directly on the document.
    </p>

    <h2>Step by step</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Sign</strong> on plain white paper with a dark pen, a bit larger than usual.</li>
      <li><strong>Photograph</strong> it from directly above, in daylight, without your phone’s shadow.</li>
      <li><strong>Open the photo here.</strong> The preview on the checkerboard shows exactly what’s transparent.</li>
      <li><strong>Adjust the slider.</strong> Go right to remove shadows and gray paper, left if thin strokes start to vanish.</li>
      <li><strong>Download.</strong> Transparent PNG for documents, or White JPG with an optional KB limit for online forms.</li>
    </ol>

    <AdSlot variant="inline" slot="tool-article" />

    <h2>Where to use the result</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Upload it in <a href="/sign-pdf">Sign PDF</a> to sign contracts and forms. It’s already clean, so it looks natural.</li>
      <li>Add it to letters and documents in Word or Google Docs.</li>
      <li>Meet signature rules on job and exam portals: <a href="/guides/photo-signature-size-for-online-applications">photo and signature size rules</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Tips for the cleanest result</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use a gel or felt-tip pen. Ballpoint ink is often too thin and gray for a crisp result.</li>
      <li>Sign in the middle of the paper, away from folds, lines and printed text.</li>
      <li>Keep the original photo. You can always re-run it with a different slider setting.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Limitations</h2>
    <p>
      It works best with dark ink on light paper. Lined or coloured paper, and signatures written in pencil, are harder to separate cleanly. It doesn’t
      straighten tilted photos, so crop or rotate first with <a href="/crop-image">Crop Image</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>Your signature should never sit on a stranger’s server. PDFSherpa processes it in your browser’s memory and forgets it when you close the tab.</p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
